(Non-Invasive Cardiac Imaging-Directed Management Versus Conventional Angiography-Based) Tj
T*
(Care in Patients With Angina and Normal Coronary Arteries: Protocol for Evaluating) Tj
T*
(Psychological and Symptom Outcomes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Patients presenting with anginal chest pain but no obstructive coronary disease often) Tj
T*
(experience persistent symptoms and psychological burden related to diagnostic uncertainty.) Tj
T*
(This protocol describes a prospective, multicenter randomized trial comparing diagnostic) Tj
T*
(and therapeutic approaches in this population. Approximately 250 participants with anginal) Tj
T*
(symptoms undergoing invasive coronary angiography showing no significant stenosis will be) Tj
T*
(randomized to one of two arms: \(1\) non-invasive stress cardiac imaging to classify disease) Tj
T*
(subtype, with treatment targeted to identified physiologic abnormality, or \(2\) standard) Tj
T*
(clinical management based on angiographic findings. Primary outcome is patient-reported) Tj
T*
(illness perception measured at 6 and 12 months using validated scales. Secondary outcomes) Tj
T*
(include psychological symptom severity, functional capacity, and symptom frequency.) Tj
T*
(Baseline psychosocial assessments will be completed, and demographic and clinical factors) Tj
T*
(will be evaluated as potential moderators. This study addresses a significant clinical gap) Tj
T*
(by evaluating whether providing diagnostic clarity via advanced imaging improves) Tj
T*
(psychological well-being.) Tj
